{
  "schema": "research-public-artifact/v1",
  "concept": "$indexStats usage statistics and their reset conditions",
  "slug": "indexstats-usage-statistics-and-their-reset-conditions",
  "canonical_concept_id": "concept:ec92a9bfeffb1c869e9681bbab37b6afc0c12c6187d8059c51484288dcf401b0",
  "canonical_artifact_sha256": "ab7b2bf03a3db2c1d6936eb0da40ad9a29c9ff1b05751e0c9ba1958fdb873783",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "clm:71feaf0ba4237a20dd1bdd15361b06b9b9d60e0fbe43d664240db77c1dc4cac5",
      "text": "Observe a representative application cycle before removing a zero-use index; infrequent reporting queries can depend on it. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.percona.com/blog/identifying-unused-indexes-in-mongodb/",
      "also": [
        "https://www.pythian.com/blog/how-to-find-unused-index-and-drop-them-safely-in-mongodb",
        "https://studio3t.com/whats-new/are-my-mongodb-indexes-being-used-studio3t_ama/",
        "https://dzone.com/articles/using-mongodb-indexstats-to-identify-and-remove-unused-indexes"
      ],
      "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED",
      "evidence_ids": []
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:5e11743e9088b6b1d7086409cbd8a6a453586ab87507bcf59c04a497067f6609",
      "text": "Store usage metrics externally when history must survive restarts. Treat any counter reset as a new observation window when comparing samples. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.percona.com/blog/identifying-unused-indexes-in-mongodb/",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/indexStats.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:8425c2a84fb3ac137dc321a4bd6f40d8455b87b8fa02df016beab2e6d7b2b039",
        "ev:b3abbc104459b511cf073feb1ab80a51357ff2448f1eb8546901f05d8a23443a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:aeb92dcc8ca8a1491a843610fb8b41dbedb9996fd24140bd6c0a8a65ef39cf0c",
      "text": "Run db.collection.aggregate([{ $indexStats: {} }]) for per-index usage documents; $indexStats must be the pipeline's first stage. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/indexStats.md",
      "also": [
        "https://studio3t.com/whats-new/are-my-mongodb-indexes-being-used-studio3t_ama/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:8d96a506f88d38430c62244932b337c5e0a02e7f95420249fbbbe89aabfac36f",
        "ev:9a251c24828546caaa7971a8dbdb469e02dfce30f5de8ec4bb1f8d00bbb91a79"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:c21b4d60d293ef5b8052d04347a8edb8a8e97efd6273d42899b3f5b15cde0124",
      "text": "accesses.ops counts user operations that used the index; accesses.since marks when MongoDB began collecting those statistics, rather than the last access time. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/indexStats.md",
      "also": [
        "https://studio3t.com/whats-new/are-my-mongodb-indexes-being-used-studio3t_ama/",
        "https://www.pythian.com/blog/how-to-find-unused-index-and-drop-them-safely-in-mongodb"
      ],
      "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED",
      "evidence_ids": []
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:ccd1479e526222996b3648a36952a8b77aa671812a9481243f280243a71310fe",
      "text": "A mongod restart resets index statistics; dropping and recreating an index also starts a new statistics window. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/indexStats.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.percona.com/blog/identifying-unused-indexes-in-mongodb/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED",
      "evidence_ids": []
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:81ff80c69becb43968b2862ab37dbce2f97ceadd6c92da0b87a87b0b5bb97726",
      "text": "Modifying an existing index through collMod resets that index's statistics; changing its hidden state is a documented example. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/indexStats.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/method/db.collection.hideIndex.md",
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/method/db.collection.unhideIndex.md",
        "https://studio3t.com/whats-new/are-my-mongodb-indexes-being-used-studio3t_ama/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:05549fe446ce9bd0fdc2a7e6f19726c01e633fa72168c0d552c17a0fbad79dec",
        "ev:b3abbc104459b511cf073feb1ab80a51357ff2448f1eb8546901f05d8a23443a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:935e43d1b896ba66f61e81184943007efa2dd199a9ad781dae2fd38942b67248",
      "text": "Hiding a visible index and unhiding a hidden index each reset its $indexStats counters. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/index-hidden.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/method/db.collection.hideIndex.md",
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/method/db.collection.unhideIndex.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED",
      "evidence_ids": []
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:1cf1737f92b3c65f650901ff37f33eee5ebb61edd5bf50939701fdaf811716bc",
      "text": "Hiding an already hidden index or unhiding an already visible index does not reset its statistics. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/index-hidden.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/method/db.collection.hideIndex.md",
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/method/db.collection.unhideIndex.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED",
      "evidence_ids": []
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:2ead379930d4baa577231868876928486d55a73c49edcc2ea13ad97c9829ff46",
      "text": "Usage statistics describe the queried node. Check all relevant replica-set members, including secondaries serving reads, before declaring an index unused. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/indexStats.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.pythian.com/blog/how-to-find-unused-index-and-drop-them-safely-in-mongodb",
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/tutorial/measure-index-use.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED",
      "evidence_ids": []
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:fedcd9e924c53df17a707808d91330ccae52f543540227ddacf486743ddb497f",
      "text": "Internal TTL deletion, chunk split, and migration operations do not increment the reported usage counters. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/indexStats.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.percona.com/blog/identifying-unused-indexes-in-mongodb/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED",
      "evidence_ids": []
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:3f743c7b35ecbf846505dda11ecac79ea5cbfd379260d9cf6e09a7b87aad67f0",
      "text": "A zero ops value does not establish that an index is unnecessary: uniqueness enforcement on insertion does not increment this counter. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.percona.com/blog/identifying-unused-indexes-in-mongodb/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:1c1060b9c5f718228dcffe2ecdf259ff365d21b5dfae4d6fdbb44afec1e2aca1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:37ec6a9dd3d5babb6d157abf806ada0a3e1de0ad214f2f49ac8119fe50f5d8ed",
      "text": "For interval monitoring, subtract two index-operation samples only while the node, index identity and statistics-start epoch remain comparable; reject intervals spanning a reset. This is a methodological inference from the documented resets. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/indexStats.md",
      "also": [
        "https://dzone.com/articles/using-mongodb-indexstats-to-identify-and-remove-unused-indexes"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:243ecdee1220b76eae932f67fbd8c627bb080ee95f1a93a30263304c49d0349b"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:5b2ffea3b25aaee2e23cda5e13f1952908e5825aa39fdb8dad42fdb98464f414",
      "text": "For a particular query, inspect explain output to establish its execution plan. $indexStats supplies aggregate usage frequency, so its counter alone does not establish that the query used SORT_MERGE. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://studio3t.com/whats-new/are-my-mongodb-indexes-being-used-studio3t_ama/",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/indexStats.md",
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/tutorial/measure-index-use.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED",
      "evidence_ids": []
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:efbf69e1e129c68250f6827b34ef0790d50a1d0e09415039908e87a5d95d5222",
      "text": "Changing an index from visible to hidden, or hidden to visible, resets its $indexStats. Hiding an already hidden index or unhiding an already visible index does not reset them. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/index-hidden.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED",
      "evidence_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "projection_sha256": "97af3050c58c39f771bae83430c96eed58d948e1f2b89b7a070aec52d59cb8ba"
}
